text:
alana: quick flag from an informal test — deep-links sometimes land the page but the left nav doesn't 'snap' to the right cluster. Keyboard users end up tabbing through controls with no nav context. breadcrumb also blinks the old route for ~250ms.

jess: can you quickly describe the snap behaviour you want?

alana: want deterministic anchoring: when external link navigates to a leaf we should 1) expand the minimal ancestor group that contains the leaf, 2) mark the leaf as active for a11y, 3) avoid forcing a full nav reflow if the user had explicitly collapsed things.

mike: implementation idea: on route resolution do a minimal diff against persisted collapse state. If navigation is external, prefer route state; if internal, preserve user collapse. Also ensure we set aria-current and apply focus to the visible nav item.

sara: accessibility checklist: role/link or role=button depending on element, aria-current=\"page\", visible focus outline (not only color), aria-live=\"polite\" message like \"Navigation: [Org] / [Model] focused\". Respect prefers-reduced-motion for any visual snap.

tom: small UX wrinkle: if we auto-expand multiple levels the nav can feel noisy. Proposal: expand only the path to the leaf (not sibling groups) and use a micro-scale slide/fade that is skip-able by reduced-motion.

jess: copy idea for breadcrumb flicker: instead of letting breadcrumb update after redirect, populate breadcrumb from resolved route data and render once. That avoids the flash. We can also show a subtle dimmed alias line under the primary label if canonicalization changes the URL.

aleah: product: favor predictability for external permalinks. Keep alias UX but canonicalize early if it prevents flicker. Add a \"Copy friendly link\" action for documentation use.

mike: technical snippet suggestion (pseudo):
```js
// router.on('restored')
const path = router.currentPath;
const node = nav.findByPath(path);
if (isExternalNav) {
  nav.expandAncestors(node);
  node.setAttribute('tabindex','0');
  node.setAttribute('aria-current','page');
  node.focus({preventScroll:true});
  // ensure nav scrolls only if item outside rails viewport
  if (!nodeIsVisibleInRail(node)) node.scrollIntoView({block:'nearest'});
}
```

sara: test cases: 1) external deep-link desktop -> nav snaps + live message, 2) external deep-link mobile drawer -> drawer opens + focus, 3) in-app navigation -> preserve collapse state, 4) reduced-motion on -> no animation. Also accessibility tests for NVDA/VoiceOver.

jess: design tokens: add variable for nav-snap-duration and nav-focus-outline-thickness. I'll push a Figma frame.

leah: experiment thought: roll out default snap for 10% of external traffic and an option in settings to toggle \"respect my collapsed nav\". Track metric: external-nav->clicks on revealed items vs immediate back.

mike: also watch for regressions: expanding many groups could cause paint spikes on low-end devices. I'll add perf guardrails (batch DOM writes, avoid forced layout).

tom: accessibility nit: when focusing the nav item we should avoid moving the main viewport abruptly. Use focus({preventScroll:true}) + localized rail scroll.

design-bot: Figma comment added: https://www.figma.com/file/xxx/leftnav-snap (comment by @jess).

alana: action items: mike implement router hook + minimal expand; sara add live region + test matrix; jess mock micro-animation + tokens; leah own experiment + copy-link action. I'll open issue #5102 with acceptance criteria and tag eng-runtime. :thumbsup:
